# The control-plane manifests this release installs, in the order they are applied.
#
# One list, two readers. The installer downloads and renders exactly these, and
# `flui env refresh-manifests` will only ADD a file that appears here — without
# that, a refresh would put back anything still sitting in this directory, and
# `05-prometheus.yaml` is sitting in this directory: it is legacy, superseded by
# VictoriaMetrics, and declares no placeholder, so every other safety rule waves
# it through. The index is what says "not part of this release" out loud.
#
# `11-zitadel` is installed only when AUTH_MODE=oidc. It is listed because the
# list describes the release, not one installation's choices; it carries a
# Secret and is therefore never eligible for a refresh anyway.
#
# Lines beginning with # are comments. Order matters to the installer.
00-secrets
01-namespace
01b-platform-priority
02-postgres
03-redis
04-vmagent-config
04a-kube-state-metrics
04b-vmagent
04c-vmalert
04d-alertmanager
05-vmsingle
06-loki
07-grafana-datasources
08-grafana
09-flui-api
12-flui-web-config
10-flui-web
11-zitadel
